# Dynamic attributes and properties

-- data attributes and methods are collectively called attributes
-- __getattr__ and __setattr__ to evaluate attribute access through dot notation
-- with __getattr__ you can implement virtual attributes -- what happens when someone calls explicitly undefined attr
-- dynamic attributes -- metaprogramming technique, you build a class from data you don't know beforehand (like json) -- get data first, then return within __getattr__
-- but data keys may not be suitable attribute names -- you can handle keywords with str.iskeyword(), invalid keys (e.g. starting with number) with str.isidentifier()

